# Claim: a variable holding an aggregate with no clone (a List of records holding a file handle, a struct or tuple holding that List, a List of such Lists) moves to its new owner at its last use, whether it is returned, rebound with `:=`, sorted in place and returned, or stored in a struct or tuple; it lowers on o0, o1 and o2 and each handle closes exactly once (Jetpack's pkg_sorted_checked_files was an ir.build ICE "a shared [CheckedFile], whose items have no clone").
# Hand-derived: gathered() opens 3 handles in the order b, c, a; sorting by name gives abc; nested() opens 2 more after the first 3 closed. "open"/"leaked" is the process's open descriptor count minus the count before the first open, so the counts are 3 while the list lives and 0 after its last owner ends.
fixture: aggregate_without_clone_moves_at_its_last_use.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read -O0 run.jet
exit: 0 # o0
stdout: = aggregate_without_clone_moves_at_its_last_use.out # o0
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read -O1 run.jet
exit: 0 # o1
stdout: = aggregate_without_clone_moves_at_its_last_use.out # o1
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read -O2 run.jet
exit: 0 # o2
stdout: = aggregate_without_clone_moves_at_its_last_use.out # o2
